"iTerm2 is sending you this message automatically because the user enabled sending terminal commands to AI for assistance. If you can provide useful non-obvious insights, respond with those. Do not restate information that is obvious from the output. If there is nothing important to say, just respond with \"Got it.\"" = "iTerm2 自动向你发送这条消息,是因为用户开启了将终端命令发送给 AI 寻求协助的功能。如果你能提供有用的非显而易见的见解,请回复这些见解。不要复述从输出中显而易见的信息。如果没有重要的内容要说,只需回复 \"Got it.\"。";
"Unknown backslash escape “%@”. Recognized: \\\\, \\n, \\r, \\t, \\uXXXX." = "未知反斜杠转义“%@”。支持的转义:\\\\、\\n、\\r、\\t、\\uXXXX。";
"Truncated \\\\uXXXX escape (needs exactly four hex digits)." = "\\uXXXX 转义被截断(需要恰好四位十六进制数字)。";
"For example, if the command so far was `git re` then you might suggest `Rewrite commit history\\tgit rebase`, `Rewrite commit history\\tgit revert`, and `Move branch pointer\\tgit reset`. " = "例如,若目前已输入的命令是 `git re`,你可以建议 `Rewrite commit history\\tgit rebase`、`Rewrite commit history\\tgit revert` 和 `Move branch pointer\\tgit reset`。 ";
"You can suggest more than one additional word when you can tell from context that it would be a good suggestion. For example, if the user frequently runs `grep ERROR <file> | sort | uniq` and you see that the text so far is `grep ERROR myfile.txt` your response could include `Count unique errors\\tgrep ERROR myfile.txt | sort | uniq`" = "当你能从上下文判断出会是好的建议时,可以建议多个补充词。例如,若用户经常运行 `grep ERROR <file> | sort | uniq` 而你看到已输入的文本是 `grep ERROR myfile.txt`,你的响应可以包含 `Count unique errors\\tgrep ERROR myfile.txt | sort | uniq`";
